<title>INDIA: India's CARE sets ratings for debt instruments.</title>
<headline>India's CARE sets ratings for debt instruments.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Analysis &amp; Research Ltd (CARE) has announced ratings for debt issues of the following companies.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p> Company		 Instrument  Rating    Issue size(Rupees)/</p>
<p>								 Comments</p>
<p>* USV Ltd.		    CP     PR1+	   (100 million)</p>
<p>* SCICI Ltd.		  Bonds  CARE AAA     (5,000 million)</p>
<p>				  PCN    CARE AAA     (13,110 million)</p>
<p>* Rajinder Steels Ltd.    NCD    CARE D	 (680 million)</p>
<p>					   (Downgraded</p>
<p>					    from CARE A+</p>
<p>					    for Rs 950 mn).</p>
<p>* Indusind Enterprises</p>
<p>  and Finance Ltd.	  FD     CARE A+(FD)  (Upto 100 million)</p>
<p>* Mukund Global Finance   FD     CARE A-(FD)  (Upto 37.50 million)</p>
<p>							    (Size enhanced</p>
<p>							     from 30 million)</p>
<p>* Ventura Guaranty Ltd.   FD     CARE BB+(FD) (Upto 5 million)</p>
<p>* National Bearing Co.</p>
<p>  (Jaipur) Ltd.	     FD     CARE BBB(FD) (Upto 1 million)</p>
<p>* TRC Financial Services  FD     CARE BBB(FD) (Upto 15 million)</p>
<p>							    (Size enhanced</p>
<p>							     from 5 million)</p>
<p>* Vijay Hemant Finance &amp;</p>
<p>  Estates Ltd.		FD     CARE BBB(FD) (Upto 80 million)</p>
<p>							    (Size enhanced</p>
<p>							     from 54 million)</p>
<p>* Mother Mira Finance &amp;</p>
<p>  Investments Ltd.	  FD     CARE BBB(FD) (Upto 34.50 million)</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>    FRB    -  Floating rate bonds</p>
<p>    CP     -  Commercial paper</p>
<p>    CD     -  Certificate of Deposit</p>
<p>    PCD    -  Partly convertible debenture</p>
<p>    FD     -  Fixed Deposit</p>
<p>    OCD    -  Optionally convertible debenture</p>
<p>    NCD    -  Non-convertible debenture</p>
<p>    PCN    -  Partly convertible notes.</p>
<p>    ICD    -  Inter Corporate Deposit</p>
<p>    CCPS   -  Cumulative convertible preference shares</p>
<p>    OFCD   -  Optionally fully convertible debentures.</p>
<p>    DDB    -  Deep Discount Bond</p>
<p>    CAR    -  Credit Analysis Rating</p>
<p>    SO     -  Structural Obligation</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>Note : PR1 is a symbol for superior, PR2 for strong, PR3 adequate, PR4 risk prone and PR5 default. The plus or minus sign after the rating indicates the relative position within the band covered by the symbol.</p>
<p>CARE AA(FD) indicates high quality, CARE A(FD) indicates adequate safety, CARE BBB(FD) indicates moderate safety, CARE AAA(FD) indicates best quality, CARE BB(FD) indicates inadequate safety, CARE B(FD) indicates risk prone, CARE C(FD) indicates high risk, and CARE D(FD) indicates default.</p>
</text>
